<section id="handoffs">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">Where it breaks</p>
        <h2>A deal changes hands a dozen times. The money leaks at the handoffs.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="sub">One new car sold touches nine departments. Most of the delay happens between them, not in the work itself.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="causes">
      <div><span class="n">01</span><h3>The same data, typed twice</h3><p>CRM to desking to Finance to the DMS, re-keyed by hand at every step.</p></div>
      <div><span class="n">02</span><h3>Handoffs nobody owns</h3><p>Each department does its part well. The work falls into the space between them.</p></div>
      <div><span class="n">03</span><h3>Deadlines nobody sees</h3><p>Contracts in transit, DMV windows, unreported units. Found at month-end, when it's too late.</p></div>
    </div>
    <h3 class="costs-title">The four that cost the most</h3>
    <div class="costs">
      <div class="cost">
        <p class="route">Marketing &rarr; BDC</p>
        <h3>Lead response</h3>
        <p>A lead arrives at 9:40 on a Saturday night and gets a call on Monday. Customers usually buy from whoever answers first.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cost">
        <p class="route">Used Cars &rarr; Parts &rarr; Service</p>
        <h3>Recon</h3>
        <p>Trades wait between stages while paying customers take the bays. Industry figures put holding cost at about $37 per unit, per day.<sup>1</sup></p>
      </div>
      <div class="cost">
        <p class="route">Finance &rarr; Billing &rarr; Lenders</p>
        <h3>Funding</h3>
        <p>Paper contracts take three to four business days to fund, and eleven to thirteen when missing stips hold them up.<sup>2</sup> Until then, the store is carrying the car.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cost">
        <p class="route">Billing &rarr; Manufacturer</p>
        <h3>Month-end reporting</h3>
        <p>A unit that's sold but not reported doesn't count toward the month's incentive target. On a stair-step program, that can cost the bonus on every car.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="srcnote"><sup>1</sup> NCM Associates 20 Group data, via <a href="https://rapidrecon.com/holding-cost-kill-your-gross/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rapid Recon</a>. <sup>2</sup> <a href="https://www.fi-magazine.com/articles/the-cit-fix" target="_blank" rel="noopener">F&amp;I and Showroom, &ldquo;The CIT Fix&rdquo;</a>.</p>
    <p class="jloop"><a href="/diagnostic/">See how the Diagnostic finds them in your store &rarr;</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

